  "notes": "Greek municipal water and sewerage bill, one fixed page. The utility name, address and emergency line at the top and the tax/page line at the bottom (\"Σελίδα 1 από 1\") are furniture. The title sits on a coloured bar together with the bill number, which is body text. Customer details and bill details are two side-by-side boxes read box by box, left first; each is a borderless key/value table with no header row. The charges table has section rows (Ύδρευση, Αποχέτευση, Φόροι) spanning all four columns and a total row whose label spans the first three columns, so the label is repeated in those cells. The tear-off payment slip below the dashed line is body text with a small key/value table. Greek decimal commas and the thousands dot in meter readings are as printed."
